 {server}←ServerLoop server;msg;TRAP;⎕TRAP
⍝ ⍵ ←→ a Server space. Changed according to my needs: Kai2#
⍝ ⎕TRAP must be localized for "C" (cut back) to work, but it must also honour
⍝ the global setting when #.ErrorParms does exist
 ⎕TNAME←'Rumba Server Loop'
 :If server.Trap
     :If 9=#.⎕NC'ErrorParms'                            ⍝ Kai2: ErrorParms must be set by caller (Plodder) if required
     :AndIf 9=##.##.⎕NC'HandleError'                    ⍝ However, in order to run Rumba's own tests we need to check this as well
         TRAP←⎕TRAP                                     ⍝ Yes, that works!
         ⎕TRAP←TRAP
         ⎕TRAP←(⊂#.ErrorParms.signal'C' '→∆CarryOn'),⎕TRAP  ⍝ HandleError signals this when it is done.
                                                             ⍝ Ours must win over an entry for the same
                                                             ⍝ event inherited from the caller (Plodder)
     :Else
         ⎕TRAP←0 'C' '→∆CarryOn'                        ⍝ No HandleError, so we can only gracefully give up
     :EndIf
 :Else
     ⎕TRAP←0 'S'
 :EndIf
 {}{
     ∇ ⍵⊣ServerWait ⍵                                   ⍝ Recursive loop
 }server
 :Return

∆CarryOn:                                               ⍝ -------------------------------------------
 ErrorInRumba server
⍝Done
